WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.051 --> 00:00:01.784
Where is your god now?

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.998
Great moment here. You see
when he's doing a cartwheel,

00:00:07.998 --> 00:00:12.000
if you do without the hands,
it gives him even more power.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.840
My name is Amen Santo.
I'm from Bahia, Brazil,

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.840
and I've been practicing
capoeira for 50 years.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.310
So today we're going to be
reviewing some capoeira scenes

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:26.260
in movies and TV and see
how effective they are.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.210
People take for granted
how powerful the hands are.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:41.160
In the modern capoeira practice,
we do have some strikes.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.890
You can use this part of your hand,

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.560
and it can hurt as much as this.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.143
If I go like this up with
full power, it's devastating.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.730
What they did is something we
do very commonly in capoeira.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:03.090
We practice the armada,

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:07.170
and typically, we get this close

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.974
to go fast and be able to react.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.220
The front kick, bênção,
that was beautifully done.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.200
Because you use your upper body
going back, you gain power.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.360
You can make someone fly like that.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.551
Wesley Snipes is an incredible guy,

00:01:26.551 --> 00:01:28.226
incredible martial artist.

00:01:28.226 --> 00:01:31.254
Because they're exaggerating,
I'll still keep it a nine.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:42.690
When we're judging by the
technical aspect, it was perfect.

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.777
Lateef is an incredible fighter.

00:01:44.777 --> 00:01:49.770
Adding that spin, right, was his choice.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:53.220
In a fighting situation,
you will never do that.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:56.550
In a lot of the presentations
you see in movies,

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.608
you can only see one part of capoeira,

00:01:59.608 --> 00:02:02.499
which is more the visual.

00:02:02.499 --> 00:02:06.480
Capoeira is an African
Brazilian martial art

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.890
and was brought from Africa to Brazil.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:15.510
But in Brazil, because of slavery,

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:19.380
people, they had to practice
capoeira differently,

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.870
because it was illegal to practice.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:25.110
So even today, people
are completely confused

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:26.668
about capoeira.

00:02:26.668 --> 00:02:29.884
Because you see, like, beautiful movement,

00:02:29.884 --> 00:02:33.360
but the whole point is to
disguise the potential you have

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.876
behind that particular movement.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:43.380
When he did the cartwheel
from the low position,

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:45.788
he had to be also careful,

00:02:45.788 --> 00:02:48.630
because if he goes all the way in,

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.113
he'll definitely hit the other actor.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.950
That one in the movie that
he kicks back and forth,

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.070
it's not a movement that
you're going to see in a fight.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:05.220
But also it gets people confused.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.550
Capoeira, there's an
element of playfulness.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.258
There's no right or wrong.

00:03:10.258 --> 00:03:12.641
Some people use more the combat,

00:03:12.641 --> 00:03:14.401
other people more the playfulness.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:24.810
That's the meia lua.
It's called half-moon.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.160
The way they were shot,

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.083
you just see the kick going like this.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:31.380
Because they do not allow
it to go all the way,

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:34.440
because it would be too
fast for him to get out.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.990
And that meia lua in the real world

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:39.270
really goes with the heel.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:42.617
With full speed, good luck with that.

00:03:42.617 --> 00:03:45.120
He wouldn't be standing up right now.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.700
I will give her nine.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.250
They were very to the point,

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:53.749
but for safety they had to
pull back a lot of stuff.

00:03:53.749 --> 00:03:55.849
Where's your god now?

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:01.505
Great moment here. You see
when he's doing a cartwheel,

00:04:01.505 --> 00:04:05.580
he's using the acrobatic
as a way of attacking.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:08.400
You can definitely generate
the cartwheel with your hands

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.230
and without your hands.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:14.190
If you do without the hands,
it gives him even more power.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:17.280
Because you're just throwing.
Your body's such a force

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.355
that it's going to swing
very hard in the face.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.820
That slide is escape.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.300
But from that escape,
typically you want to strike,

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.730
because what you do after the escape,

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:33.690
that's the whole point.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:37.440
The nature of capoeira, you
escape and you have a follow-up.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.720
From that situation, you're dodging,

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.120
then I will throw a meia lua,

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.660
which is a low kick.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:49.402
Can be anywhere, from the
leg, here, or up to the head.

00:04:52.159 --> 00:04:53.534
No powers!

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:02.010
So, that's one very, very typical
way of attacking capoeira,

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.158
is with a headbutt.

00:05:03.158 --> 00:05:04.680
And they're doing the different angles,

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.430
like forward, sideways, backwards.

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:09.796
But this was perfect because

00:05:09.796 --> 00:05:12.020
the only way he can actually strike back

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:13.700
was using his headbutt.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:19.110
And that was a perfect example,

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.730
where he did that scissor.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:24.600
It was beautifully done because
it comes from the ground,

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:28.000
which is, capoeira, I
think, is the only art

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:31.530
that we really use the
floor the way we do.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:35.280
Equally, 50/50, standing
and also using the ground.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:37.380
And then he went to the choking,

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.270
which is more like jujitsu.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:43.470
Definitely the capoeira
scissor allowed the person

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:45.840
to have the opportunity
to do the next thing.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:48.390
There were certain things that
I would've done differently,

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:52.265
like the escapes. I'll give a seven.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:05:59.913
It can be very fluid.

00:05:59.913 --> 00:06:03.420
It can be from slow pace to superfast

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:07.620
and do, like, five, six, seven,
eight kicks back-to-back.

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:09.930
It can be super dangerous when you do that

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.005
and when you have the right timing.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:20.640
With that lower position that
we call rasteira, the sweep,

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:24.780
it can be done but will be extremely hard.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:28.020
Especially if you have
someone like Batman.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.420
She will be more in advantage

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:33.828
of waiting for him to attack her

00:06:33.828 --> 00:06:36.336
and be responding

00:06:36.336 --> 00:06:38.910
instead of being attacking all the time.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:43.380
And using techniques
that would hit the chin,

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.855
be more direct, the groin,

00:06:45.855 --> 00:06:48.929
the knee, throat, eye.

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:58.530
She used the walls to kick.

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:00.120
Visually, it's great.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.810
When you telegraph, when you
show what you're going to do,

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:07.080
that means your opponent
will be ready to respond.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.200
It's not the capoeira nature of showing.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.190
Like a snake,

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:15.000
and a snake will wait for
the right moment to go.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.220
I will give you a 4 ½.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:18.148
Wait, what is it?

00:07:18.148 --> 00:07:19.350
It's capoeira.

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:20.580
I thought maybe you were doing it wrong,

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.380
but that's actually what it looks like.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:26.765
If you're practicing this,
you know, calling ginga,

00:07:26.765 --> 00:07:28.062
you know, that's silly.

00:07:28.062 --> 00:07:29.880
If I'm practicing ginga,

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:34.380
basically it's the stance, you
know, you do your triangle.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:37.555
I'm working my posture

00:07:37.555 --> 00:07:39.771
so I can block with my elbow.

00:07:39.771 --> 00:07:42.600
I can block down, I can block up.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.263
So you move, you escape,
attack from that foundation.

00:07:46.263 --> 00:07:49.110
If you're just there doing this all day,

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.612
it's pretty funny.

00:07:50.612 --> 00:07:53.545
Jairo: Ha! Sa! Sha! Brazil!

00:07:53.545 --> 00:07:55.980
Sa! Sha! Brazil!

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:58.588
Even this entrance here

00:07:58.588 --> 00:08:01.263
is more like a karate entrance.

00:08:01.263 --> 00:08:03.720
Just imagine someone, like, doing karate

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:07.211
and doing cartwheels and, "Ha! Huh! Huh!"

00:08:07.211 --> 00:08:09.274
It's interesting.

00:08:09.274 --> 00:08:13.350
But it's definitely not a representation

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:15.683
of what we're talking about.

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:20.767
My name is Jairo. Welcome
to the world of capoeira.

00:08:20.767 --> 00:08:23.970
Capoeira is the most seductive
form of self-defense.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:27.150
It combines peacefulness,
fighting, and cardio.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:28.440
Hold there for a second.

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:31.090
Peacefulness,

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:35.673
this, to me, it feels like more like yoga.

00:08:35.673 --> 00:08:37.950
Capoeira came from struggles,

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.250
came from a survival situation.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:44.850
To be peaceful when
you're supposed to survive

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:48.690
is a contradiction there.

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:50.550
Jairo: You can advance through the stages

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:53.192
by earning different-colored chords at the

00:08:53.192 --> 00:08:55.410
troca de cordoes.

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:57.668
The rankings, right?

00:08:57.668 --> 00:09:02.518
That became more popular

00:09:02.518 --> 00:09:03.559
later on,

00:09:03.559 --> 00:09:06.300
but that traditionally wasn't that way.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:09.870
Lots of the training
were done in the streets.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:11.818
Because certain people,

00:09:11.818 --> 00:09:15.059
they were able to survive

00:09:15.059 --> 00:09:17.433
doing this combat,

00:09:17.433 --> 00:09:21.841
they became recognized as a master

00:09:21.841 --> 00:09:25.080
or a teacher by the community

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.930
instead of someone just
giving you a ranking.

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:29.971
I'll give 1 ½.

00:09:37.722 --> 00:09:39.580
That was a great way

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:42.696
to use capoeira, with lasers.

00:09:42.696 --> 00:09:45.810
He's using a lot of capoeira Angola.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.670
There are two styles capoeira.

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:51.450
Capoeira Angola, which
you're going to see a lot

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:55.440
of the more fluid, slow movements.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:58.320
Some people can stand up
as well, but most people,

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:00.630
they'll be more on the
lower part of the art.

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:03.480
The other style is
called capoeira regional.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.121
That was introduced later

00:10:05.121 --> 00:10:09.254
by a master called Mestre Bimba,

00:10:09.254 --> 00:10:11.730
which you're going to see more the strikes

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:13.860
like the other films that you saw.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:15.540
And it's interesting, this scene here,

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:20.100
that they use a lot of that
to avoid to be touched,

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:22.980
not to be in control of anything,

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.280
and just react to something that you see.

00:10:30.974 --> 00:10:34.860
To be able to fall and
be able to bounce back

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.350
without putting a lot of effort,

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:41.100
did a good job as far
as using the flexibility

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:45.300
and the abilities that we
are capable of in capoeira.

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:47.027
I'll give 8 ½.

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:54.870
This is me when I used to have long hair.

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:58.830
People think that we're actually
doing the fighting here.

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:01.088
We are doing the roda circle

00:11:01.088 --> 00:11:04.146
to practice our skills.

00:11:04.146 --> 00:11:07.110
If you notice, there's no contact,

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:09.402
because it is more the training.

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:18.990
So, the music is a big part of capoeira.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:23.983
Basically, in a circle,
you have a bateria.

00:11:23.983 --> 00:11:28.020
That means where they have
the berimbau, the drum.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:31.380
So when you clap and when
you sing and when you play,

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:33.330
you create more and more energy,

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.640
so you'll be able to perform better.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:37.680
Even during slavery, a lot of times,

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:42.609
the music was used to create
courage, to create endurance,

00:11:42.609 --> 00:11:45.360
to be able to fight
against the oppressors.

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:48.240
So the musicality is so important.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:52.800
Talks about history, it
talks about struggles,

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:56.823
how we were able to overcome
to become who we are today.

00:11:56.823 --> 00:12:01.787
I think this film was the first movie

00:12:01.787 --> 00:12:06.000
that actually featured
capoeira from beginning to end.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:09.240
I won't give it 10, I will give 9 ½,

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.940
because I know there was
a lot of way to improve.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:18.794
Will Ferrell is such a funny guy.

00:12:18.794 --> 00:12:22.980
I think the capoeira here is
definitely overly exaggerated.

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:25.238
You don't need to go over,

00:12:25.238 --> 00:12:27.030
but in a real situation

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:30.870
he just simply has to go
down and then drop the kick.

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:34.950
If you're going to spend that
time just flying in the air,

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:37.903
before you drop, people
can, they have many options

00:12:37.903 --> 00:12:39.995
to get out of the way and do other things.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.980
Would it be interesting
if it was the berimbau

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:49.116
and he was hitting people?

00:12:49.116 --> 00:12:51.360
Then it would be very accurate.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:56.340
The berimbau is the main
instrument in capoeira.

00:12:56.340 --> 00:13:00.690
But using somebody's body to do that

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:02.790
is pretty unrealistic.

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:06.000
This one I'll rate 6 ½.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.670
It's too much of an exaggeration

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:11.515
to complete one simple task.

00:13:14.933 --> 00:13:16.560
OK, let's stop!

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.260
Historically, it's a great story,

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:21.235
but it took it to a level

00:13:21.235 --> 00:13:24.626
that for me was unnecessary.

00:13:24.626 --> 00:13:27.720
Besouro was an incredible capoeirista.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:31.530
Traditionally, people claimed
that he was able to fly.

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:34.350
And it's very romantic.

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:38.730
But this scene here,
completely unrealistic.

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:40.290
How can somebody be shooting

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.180
and you be flying in the air like that?

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:44.614
I can watch "The Matrix"
and appreciate that.

00:13:44.614 --> 00:13:47.015
It's a whole different story here.

00:13:51.392 --> 00:13:54.930
Even though you have
three people with rifles,

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:56.760
and you still be able to stand up.

00:13:56.760 --> 00:13:58.770
Not very realistic, but it's doable.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.810
Capoeira came from that environment,

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:02.280
fighting multiple people.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:04.978
It is just something that we know works.

00:14:04.978 --> 00:14:08.232
But, again, it depends how good you are,

00:14:08.232 --> 00:14:12.735
how effective you are, how efficient,

00:14:12.735 --> 00:14:14.760
and that goes with many other arts,

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:16.635
you know, not just capoeira.

00:14:16.635 --> 00:14:18.690
I will give it a four.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:21.930
My favorite movie featuring capoeira,

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:25.830
not because I'm in it, but
I think "Only the Strong"

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:30.000
because there was the
element of the performance

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:34.470
and now the actual
combat to be able to use

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:36.600
in a full-length film.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.340
Thanks for watching this video.

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:41.840
If you like this one, watch the one above.

